### Step 7: Calculate MoC & Downturn Coefficient

#### MoC Calculation

$$\text{MoC} = \text{LGD}_{\text{DT}} - \text{LRA}$$

```python
def calcule_moc(lgd_dt: float, lra: float) -> float:
    """MoC = difference between downturn LGD and LRA."""
    moc = lgd_dt - lra
    return moc

moc_value = calcule_moc(lgd_dt=0.431, lra=0.357)
# moc_value = 0.074 (7.4 percentage points)
```

#### Downturn Coefficient

$$\text{Coef}_{\text{DT}} = \frac{\text{LGD}_{\text{DT}} - \text{LRA}}{\text{LRA}} = \frac{\text{MoC}}{\text{LRA}}$$

```python
def calcule_downturn(df_final: pl.DataFrame) -> pl.DataFrame:
    """
    Calculate downturn coefficient and final LGD.
    """
    coef_dt = (df_final['lgd_dt'] - df_final['lra_globale']) / df_final['lra_globale']
    downturn_val = coef_dt * df_final['lra_globale']
    lgd_downturn = df_final['lgd_dt'] + downturn_val
    
    return pl.DataFrame({
        "Segment": df_final["segment"],
        "LGD DT": df_final['lgd_dt'],
        "LRA": df_final['lra_globale'],
        "Coefficient Downturn": coef_dt,
        "Downturn": downturn_val,
        "LGD downturn": lgd_downturn,
        "Significatif": df_final['significatif'],
    })
```

