## 12. Appendices

### Appendix A: Formula Reference

#### LRA (Long-Run Average)
$$\text{LRA}_{\text{simple}} = \frac{1}{n} \sum_{i=1}^{n} \text{LGD}_i$$

$$\text{LRA}_{\text{weighted}} = \frac{\sum_{j} \overline{\text{LGD}}_j \cdot n_j}{\sum_{j} n_j}$$

#### t-test Statistic
$$t = \frac{\bar{x} - \text{LRA}}{s / \sqrt{n}}, \quad t \sim t_{n-1}$$

#### One-Tailed p-value
$$p_{1\text{-tail}} = P(T_{n-1} > t_{\text{obs}}) = \begin{cases} p_{2\text{-tail}} / 2 & t > 0 \\ 1 & t \le 0 \end{cases}$$

#### MoC
$$\text{MoC} = \text{LGD}_{\text{DT}} - \text{LRA}$$

#### Downturn Coefficient
$$\text{Coef}_{\text{DT}} = \frac{\text{MoC}}{\text{LRA}} = \frac{\text{LGD}_{\text{DT}} - \text{LRA}}{\text{LRA}}$$

#### Regulatory RWA (Simplified)
$$\text{RWA} = \text{EAD} \times K(\text{PD}, \text{LGD}_{\text{DT}}, \text{Maturity})$$

where $K$ is the IRB formula incorporating downturn LGD.

